    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1159">

                <pb facs="0955" n="839" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg839"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.11/862.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Ambassador to the Secretary of
                    State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-09-10T18:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 10, 1912—6 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Department’s No. 906, September 5, transmitting note to be delivered to Mexican
                    Foreign Office. I recommend reference in the note to the arrest and imprisonment
                    of Americans in filthy jails on frivolous charges, and the refusal of bail in
                    such cases; also reference to the case of the American railway men. If
                    Department does not think these changes advisable I shall present note without
                    alteration.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
